Round-5 claude-fable-5 attempt on ls20 explored a different route than
round 3's pinwheel/lower-pad line -- a lower-left ring approach. Reached
the exact required target shape with color E one pinwheel entry away from
color 8, but the return route failed: the lower ring cell cannot move
left directly, it must move up twice then left before ascending. That
navigation mistake exhausted the step counter before the pinwheel.

Honest null -- no registry count change, frontier stays at level 4.
Round-3's "insert the upper black-dot selector" hypothesis remains
untested by this route.

